# 128-node 8:1 oversubscribed 3-tier fat tree
# Paper setup: 800Gbps, 400ns switch latency, 600ns link latency
# 2 pods x 64 hosts/pod = 128 nodes
# ToR: 8 down (hosts) + 1 up = 8:1 OS. AGG: 8 down + 8 up. Core: 2 down.
# no_of_tor_uplinks = 128*800/(800*8) = 16
# agg_switches_per_pod = radix_up[TOR]/bundlesize[AGG] = 1/1 = 1
# no_of_agg_uplinks = 16*800/(800*1) = 16
# no_of_core_switches = 16/2 = 8
# AGG up-radix check: (8*1)/1 = 8 = radix_up[AGG] OK
Nodes 128
Tiers 3
Podsize 64

Tier 0
Oversubscribed 8
Downlink_speed_Gbps 800
Radix_Down 8
Radix_Up 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 600
Switch_Latency_ns 400

Tier 1
Oversubscribed 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 800
Radix_Down 8
Radix_Up 8
Downlink_Latency_ns 600
Switch_Latency_ns 400
Bundle 1

Tier 2
Downlink_speed_Gbps 800
Radix_Down 2
Downlink_Latency_ns 600
Switch_Latency_ns 400
Bundle 1
